# Bayesian Updating

## Bayesian Updating: What it is not {notes="notes/week1_notes.md#what-it-is-not"}
![*Statistical Rethinking*, p.2 (Richard McElreath, 2020)](images/week1/mcelreath-2.png){fig-align="center" width="100%"}

## Bayesian Updating: What it is {notes="notes/week1_notes.md#bayesian-updating"}

Instead of a flowchart of tests, updating is [**one rule for all of statistics**]{.blue}:

[**Prior**]{.red} × [**Likelihood**]{.blue} → [**Posterior**]{.green}

::: {.incremental}
- [**Prior**]{.red}: what we believed _before_ the new data
- [**Likelihood**]{.blue}: for _each_ possible answer, how expected were the data we saw?
- [**Posterior**]{.green}: what we believe _now_, with the new data taken into account
:::

::: {.fragment .callout-tip title="Example: will the mayor win?"}
::: {.incremental}
- [**Prior**]{.red}: _"The mayor got 60% of the vote last time, so I think about 60% will vote for them again."_
- [**Likelihood**]{.blue}: _"In my small survey, only 20% of people said they'll vote for the mayor. That would be surprising if the mayor's true support were 60%, but quite likely if it were around 20–30%."_
- [**Posterior**]{.green}: _"Based on this new data, I now think it's probably around 40–50%."_
:::
::: {.fragment }
If we decide to gather more data, our posterior becomes the prior for future observations.
:::
:::

## You already understand Bayesian updating {notes="notes/week1_notes.md#already-updated"}

_Both of today's examples were updates. We just hadn't named the parts._

|  | The HIV test | 1,000 ideas |
|---|---|---|
| [**Prior**]{.red} | Before the test:<br>0.1% chance of HIV | Before the study:<br>1% chance it's true |
| [[**Likelihood**]{.blue}]{.fragment fragment-index=1} | [Positive:<br>99% if HIV+, 3% if HIV–]{.fragment fragment-index=1} | [Significant:<br>80% if true, 5% if false]{.fragment fragment-index=1} |
| [[**Posterior**]{.green}]{.fragment fragment-index=2} | [After a positive: 3%]{.fragment fragment-index=2} | [After a significant result: 14%]{.fragment fragment-index=2} |
| [[**A different prior**]{.red}]{.fragment fragment-index=3} | [Start at 10% → 79%]{.fragment fragment-index=3} | [Start at 10% → 64%]{.fragment fragment-index=3} |

: {tbl-colwidths="[20,40,40]"}

::: {.fragment fragment-index=4}
Clouds in July? You grab an umbrella. That's updating.
:::

::: {.fragment fragment-index=5}
You've updated all your life. Statistics does it out loud, so others can check.
:::

